1
00:00:50,669 --> 00:00:53,964
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:54,673 --> 00:00:55,882
Ms. Da-reum.

3
00:00:56,424 --> 00:00:58,301
I'm not into men.

4
00:00:59,052 --> 00:01:00,303
- What?
- Also...

5
00:01:02,138 --> 00:01:03,932
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

6
00:01:05,725 --> 00:01:06,768
What?

7
00:01:38,341 --> 00:01:39,384
Director Lee.

8
00:01:39,926 --> 00:01:41,011
How did you find us here?

9
00:01:51,813 --> 00:01:52,981
I heard about the covert op.

10
00:01:53,898 --> 00:01:56,776
Ms. Kim told me that you had trouble
trying to get Master Im on board.

11
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:58,445
I came out to help.

12
00:01:59,237 --> 00:02:00,238
At this hour?

13
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:01,823
Did you really come for work?

14
00:02:01,906 --> 00:02:04,701
Of course.
I'm that serious about work.

15
00:02:11,207 --> 00:02:12,250
So, well...

16
00:02:12,876 --> 00:02:14,878
There are only two rooms.

17
00:02:15,086 --> 00:02:16,504
I can crash in his room.

18
00:02:17,505 --> 00:02:19,799
- You, in my room?
- It's not like I can take her room.

19
00:02:22,052 --> 00:02:24,054
Well, that wasn't what I meant.

20
00:02:24,304 --> 00:02:26,264
It's nothing new between us.

21
00:02:30,685 --> 00:02:31,770
Get away from me.

22
00:02:35,482 --> 00:02:38,026
I won't misunderstand
the situation anymore, Mr. Kang.

23
00:02:38,109 --> 00:02:39,110
Don't worry.

24
00:02:39,653 --> 00:02:40,654
"Misunderstand"?

25
00:02:41,071 --> 00:02:43,365
Well, if it's
too inconvenient for you

26
00:02:43,448 --> 00:02:45,742
I can sleep out in the hall.

27
00:02:46,076 --> 00:02:48,411
No, you should take one of the rooms.

28
00:02:48,787 --> 00:02:50,538
- I'll share mine with him.
- Okay.

29
00:02:51,247 --> 00:02:52,624
Okay. Then it's decided.

30
00:02:52,874 --> 00:02:53,917
We'll take this one.

31
00:02:55,502 --> 00:02:58,505
- Good night.
- Have a good rest.

32
00:03:13,353 --> 00:03:15,522
You have a thing
for Director Lee Chan.

33
00:03:15,605 --> 00:03:18,316
For a long time.

34
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:21,903
I mean, me?

35
00:03:23,571 --> 00:03:25,740
- Jeez.
- Da-reum is unbelievable.

36
00:03:25,824 --> 00:03:28,451
What about me gives off that vibe?

37
00:03:34,999 --> 00:03:36,543
Are you disappointed

38
00:03:36,793 --> 00:03:38,044
that she doesn't think of you
as a man?

39
00:03:38,128 --> 00:03:39,129
Whatever.

40
00:03:40,004 --> 00:03:41,005
Gosh.

41
00:03:46,886 --> 00:03:47,887
I can tell

42
00:03:49,431 --> 00:03:51,015
that you care about Da-reum.

43
00:03:52,475 --> 00:03:53,810
Concerned? Hardly.

44
00:03:55,687 --> 00:03:57,230
She's new to work.

45
00:03:57,313 --> 00:03:58,606
That's why I'm looking out for her.

46
00:04:03,027 --> 00:04:05,655
Looking out for someone and actually
caring for them aren't the same.

47
00:04:07,407 --> 00:04:08,491
It's different.

48
00:04:20,378 --> 00:04:21,713
Wait, Ms. Nam.

49
00:04:23,965 --> 00:04:25,592
- What?
- Also...

50
00:04:26,468 --> 00:04:28,178
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

51
00:04:30,513 --> 00:04:31,514
What?

52
00:04:46,321 --> 00:04:48,364
I could see today
that you two have grown close.

53
00:04:49,407 --> 00:04:52,118
I had a feeling
that you might be interested in her.

54
00:04:54,913 --> 00:04:55,914
I'm not.

55
00:04:57,165 --> 00:04:58,208
Even if I did

56
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:01,002
it's impossible for a CEO
to date a rookie.

57
00:05:22,899 --> 00:05:25,652
So Mr. Kang wasn't into men.

58
00:05:27,403 --> 00:05:30,490
Who's the woman he's interested in?

59
00:05:39,791 --> 00:05:40,959
Come on, Da-reum.

60
00:05:41,501 --> 00:05:44,587
Why do you want to know that?

61
00:05:45,004 --> 00:05:46,130
Come on.

62
00:05:48,508 --> 00:05:51,177
Could it be someone at work?

63
00:06:35,305 --> 00:06:37,056
Yes, just like that.

64
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:38,182
Don't let it get tangled.

65
00:06:38,266 --> 00:06:40,018
Like that.

66
00:06:40,101 --> 00:06:42,186
That's it. Carefully.

67
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:43,646
Okay. Good.

68
00:06:46,691 --> 00:06:47,775
You have a knack for this.

69
00:06:52,947 --> 00:06:54,490
Did you have trouble sleeping too?

70
00:06:56,075 --> 00:06:57,118
Yes.

71
00:06:57,827 --> 00:06:59,370
And I saw the light was on.

72
00:07:00,955 --> 00:07:02,248
Come here and join me.

73
00:07:04,876 --> 00:07:05,877
May I?

74
00:07:09,213 --> 00:07:12,050
It's best to move your hands
when you're stressed out.

75
00:07:12,675 --> 00:07:14,552
Knotting may seem like a job
where you tie things

76
00:07:14,636 --> 00:07:17,513
but you'll come to learn
that it can untangle your heart.

77
00:07:18,681 --> 00:07:21,684
You're right.
Tying knots helped me clear my head.

78
00:07:23,853 --> 00:07:25,980
- You should give it a go too.
- Okay.

79
00:07:26,230 --> 00:07:28,024
- Do what you did yesterday.
- Okay.

80
00:07:35,823 --> 00:07:38,534
I let my feelings
get ahead of me yesterday.

81
00:07:39,035 --> 00:07:40,620
I shouldn't have said it like that.

82
00:07:42,997 --> 00:07:45,708
So even if Master Im
doesn't agree to be on board

83
00:07:46,167 --> 00:07:49,212
I hope you two can make
these traditional knots more visible.

84
00:07:51,589 --> 00:07:54,258
We completely understand
what you mean.

85
00:07:55,927 --> 00:07:58,972
I'm happy to know that you do.

86
00:08:00,473 --> 00:08:02,767
Please continue to practice.
I'll get breakfast ready.

87
00:08:03,142 --> 00:08:04,811
- Sure.
- And this one.

88
00:08:05,186 --> 00:08:06,646
I'm taking your first knot.

89
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:15,363
Ta-da. I made a new one.

90
00:08:15,613 --> 00:08:16,948
I learned it just now.

91
00:08:17,031 --> 00:08:19,200
- You've learned it already?
- Yes.

92
00:08:20,159 --> 00:08:22,203
Do you want me to teach you?

93
00:08:22,829 --> 00:08:23,871
Sure.

94
00:08:24,288 --> 00:08:25,331
Let's do it.

95
00:08:26,207 --> 00:08:28,292
All right. Take a good look.

96
00:08:28,835 --> 00:08:31,587
Put the green cord
on top of the pink one

97
00:08:32,005 --> 00:08:33,965
and create a knot.

98
00:08:34,590 --> 00:08:37,802
Good. Now do you see this space here?

99
00:08:37,885 --> 00:08:39,679
Spread it out a little.

100
00:08:39,762 --> 00:08:41,681
Look, it's a heart.

101
00:08:43,975 --> 00:08:49,230
Then hold the top
and make a wing on each side.

102
00:08:49,939 --> 00:08:52,025
- A wing...
- Yes.

103
00:08:53,317 --> 00:08:56,612
Then hold the top
and pull it to the side.

104
00:09:20,303 --> 00:09:23,389
The young lady
who came from Seoul made this.

105
00:09:24,766 --> 00:09:26,184
She tried rather hard

106
00:09:26,893 --> 00:09:27,977
after just one day.

107
00:09:35,068 --> 00:09:36,527
Isn't that admirable?

108
00:09:41,991 --> 00:09:42,992
Master Im.

109
00:09:44,202 --> 00:09:46,496
I apologize for yesterday.

110
00:09:47,872 --> 00:09:50,124
I knew your intentions very well.

111
00:09:54,253 --> 00:09:55,838
It's always tough

112
00:09:57,298 --> 00:09:58,591
to be a teacher.

113
00:09:59,175 --> 00:10:01,886
I must always keep an eye
on people's feelings as I proceed...

114
00:10:04,847 --> 00:10:06,307
but at times,
I find myself blurting out words

115
00:10:07,517 --> 00:10:08,976
that can turn into sharp blades.

116
00:10:12,230 --> 00:10:13,314
Are you

117
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:15,525
apologizing right now?

118
00:10:25,118 --> 00:10:27,411
I was just afraid.

119
00:10:28,246 --> 00:10:32,416
That everything we have stood for
would disappear down that road.

120
00:10:40,508 --> 00:10:42,635
It won't disappear, Master Im.

121
00:11:13,416 --> 00:11:14,667
How beautiful.

122
00:11:17,003 --> 00:11:18,212
These are so pretty.

123
00:11:21,132 --> 00:11:22,633
When did you come out?

124
00:11:24,177 --> 00:11:25,178
Just now.

125
00:11:25,845 --> 00:11:28,389
They looked so pretty from the window

126
00:11:28,931 --> 00:11:30,349
so I came out to see them up close.

127
00:11:46,699 --> 00:11:49,160
I'm sorry for that day.

128
00:11:51,287 --> 00:11:54,957
It had been weighing on my mind
after you left like that.

129
00:11:59,253 --> 00:12:00,338
Please don't mind me.

130
00:12:01,088 --> 00:12:03,674
You suffered from a misunderstanding
because of me.

131
00:12:04,133 --> 00:12:05,343
It must've put you in a tough spot.

132
00:12:06,928 --> 00:12:08,596
She and I had already broken up.

133
00:12:09,972 --> 00:12:11,307
She must've said

134
00:12:11,974 --> 00:12:14,268
all those mean things to you
out of spite for me.

135
00:12:15,770 --> 00:12:16,896
I apologize.

136
00:12:20,107 --> 00:12:21,901
I'm really fine.

137
00:12:28,199 --> 00:12:30,117
I'm okay, really.

138
00:12:37,208 --> 00:12:38,251
Da-reum.

139
00:12:38,584 --> 00:12:40,503
There's something I want to show you.

140
00:12:41,921 --> 00:12:45,216
Can you spare me some time
on our way back to Seoul?

141
00:12:55,601 --> 00:12:57,144
A lot went through my mind

142
00:12:58,062 --> 00:12:59,522
after learning how to make knots.

143
00:13:00,439 --> 00:13:02,692
Traditional knots
are a form of art and meditation

144
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:04,860
not something
you can print with a machine.

145
00:13:05,569 --> 00:13:07,697
I brought up words
like factory production

146
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:09,573
without realizing
how deep the practice was.

147
00:13:12,368 --> 00:13:13,369
I apologize.

148
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,413
I apologize.

149
00:13:16,706 --> 00:13:18,541
And because we desperately
wanted to work with you

150
00:13:19,041 --> 00:13:20,918
I also had forgotten
about the core of my business.

151
00:13:21,544 --> 00:13:23,629
Appello strives
to maintain value that will last

152
00:13:24,755 --> 00:13:26,549
instead of fast-paced trends.

153
00:13:28,217 --> 00:13:30,344
So what if we provided
an experience for the people

154
00:13:30,761 --> 00:13:33,723
in the exact traditional way
of your practice?

155
00:13:42,940 --> 00:13:46,277
How about putting together a DIY kit

156
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,154
so people can try making
traditional Korean knots

157
00:13:48,237 --> 00:13:51,657
with all the materials
and instructions at home?

158
00:13:52,658 --> 00:13:55,161
I thought
it was very difficult to make knots

159
00:13:55,244 --> 00:13:57,496
but I had so much fun
when I got my hands on it.

160
00:13:57,830 --> 00:14:00,124
I'm sure many people will love it.

161
00:14:10,343 --> 00:14:12,053
Perhaps it's more meaningful

162
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:16,015
to have knots
created by many new hands

163
00:14:18,517 --> 00:14:21,437
instead of ones made
by a single artisan.

164
00:14:23,230 --> 00:14:26,317
If you're going to make it,
make it right.

165
00:14:26,817 --> 00:14:28,277
The traditional knot kit.

166
00:14:31,072 --> 00:14:32,198
Thank you, Master Im.

167
00:14:32,281 --> 00:14:34,533
- Thank you, ma'am.
- However...

168
00:14:35,493 --> 00:14:36,702
there is one condition.

169
00:14:37,411 --> 00:14:40,998
I won't allow you to make something
with half-hearted instructions.

170
00:14:41,248 --> 00:14:42,958
They must have hands-on experience

171
00:14:44,168 --> 00:14:46,128
as they learn to make actual knots.

172
00:14:47,463 --> 00:14:50,341
Do you mean that people must
take part in the experience?

173
00:14:51,050 --> 00:14:52,635
That's what will actually last.

174
00:14:53,344 --> 00:14:54,887
I'll see what you come up with

175
00:14:54,970 --> 00:14:57,473
before I go ahead
and give you my final approval.

176
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:16,617
- Hop in, Ms. Nam.
- Okay.

177
00:15:17,201 --> 00:15:19,036
Ms. Da-reum, let's go in my car.

178
00:15:20,162 --> 00:15:21,497
You'd probably prefer to go alone.

179
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,917
Come with me. His car
isn't built for long-distance trips.

180
00:15:25,751 --> 00:15:28,796
What do you mean?
I'd get there an hour before you.

181
00:15:30,381 --> 00:15:31,424
Hey.

182
00:15:32,133 --> 00:15:34,009
My seats come with a massager.

183
00:15:35,636 --> 00:15:37,513
You can lie down flat on my seat.

184
00:15:44,061 --> 00:15:45,396
Ms. Da-reum,
whose car do you want to take?

185
00:15:48,774 --> 00:15:51,068
First of all,
can you let my hands go?

186
00:15:57,867 --> 00:15:58,909
Then...

187
00:16:01,245 --> 00:16:02,997
I'm sorry for that day.

188
00:16:03,706 --> 00:16:05,833
There's something I want to show you.

189
00:16:05,958 --> 00:16:07,376
Can you spare me some time

190
00:16:07,918 --> 00:16:09,420
on our way back to Seoul?

191
00:16:13,299 --> 00:16:14,550
May I take

192
00:16:15,092 --> 00:16:16,969
Director Lee's car?

193
00:16:17,052 --> 00:16:18,679
You'll also find
that more convenient.

194
00:16:21,223 --> 00:16:22,308
All right, then.

195
00:16:25,561 --> 00:16:26,979
Was my car uncomfortable?

196
00:16:28,606 --> 00:16:31,817
No, it was such a comfortable ride.

197
00:16:31,901 --> 00:16:35,196
I just felt bad
that you always had to give me rides.

198
00:16:38,574 --> 00:16:40,826
I'll take Ms. Da-reum home.

199
00:16:44,455 --> 00:16:45,789
Have a safe trip back.

200
00:16:47,875 --> 00:16:49,084
Thank you.

201
00:16:54,757 --> 00:16:55,841
Hey, Ha-gi.

202
00:16:56,884 --> 00:16:57,968
Drive safely.

203
00:16:58,552 --> 00:16:59,637
Sure.

204
00:17:12,399 --> 00:17:13,734
Do you know where you are?

205
00:17:16,779 --> 00:17:19,865
It's a bus stop in my neighborhood.

206
00:17:27,289 --> 00:17:29,083
D.N.X FOREVER
LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER

207
00:17:29,333 --> 00:17:30,584
Oh, this...

208
00:17:31,835 --> 00:17:33,003
You wrote this.

209
00:17:34,255 --> 00:17:35,714
How did you know that?

210
00:17:39,677 --> 00:17:40,928
Do you remember this photo book?

211
00:17:43,806 --> 00:17:45,349
This is...

212
00:17:58,445 --> 00:17:59,530
Chan.

213
00:18:04,076 --> 00:18:05,869
EXCLUSIVE:
WHERE IS D.N.X'S LEE CHAN NOW?

214
00:18:08,706 --> 00:18:09,957
DISAPPEARED AFTER THEY DISBANDED

215
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,166
D.N.X DISBANDS AFTER 3 YEARS

216
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:17,881
I can't believe D.N.X still has fans.

217
00:18:18,382 --> 00:18:19,883
I thought they were over.

218
00:18:19,967 --> 00:18:22,553
- Be quiet.
- I'm not wrong.

219
00:18:22,636 --> 00:18:24,263
I feel bad for her.

220
00:18:24,930 --> 00:18:26,140
It must be embarrassing.

221
00:18:44,325 --> 00:18:46,910
D.N.X FOREVER
WE WILL BE TOGETHER FOREVER

222
00:18:46,994 --> 00:18:49,330
"DESTINY NEVER X,"
I KNOW I'LL SEE YOU ON STAGE AGAIN

223
00:18:54,627 --> 00:18:57,087
I can't believe you still had this.

224
00:18:58,130 --> 00:19:00,257
When I was going through
the toughest time after we disbanded

225
00:19:01,258 --> 00:19:03,385
this journal helped me stay strong.

226
00:19:08,974 --> 00:19:12,811
I didn't expect you
to hold this so dearly.

227
00:19:14,605 --> 00:19:17,900
During those toughest days,
I went and looked for these places.

228
00:19:22,071 --> 00:19:23,572
I thought I'd perhaps see you.

229
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:36,085
D.N.X FOREVER
LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER

230
00:19:38,295 --> 00:19:41,048
D.N.X FOREVER
LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER

231
00:19:54,478 --> 00:19:55,604
The person who continued

232
00:19:56,563 --> 00:19:58,190
to show me their support somewhere.

233
00:20:02,403 --> 00:20:03,696
And now, we've finally met.

234
00:20:12,579 --> 00:20:14,623
This is fascinating.

235
00:20:16,792 --> 00:20:19,461
I also spent
a lot of time sitting here

236
00:20:19,962 --> 00:20:21,672
listening to your songs

237
00:20:22,089 --> 00:20:23,841
just trying to get through life.

238
00:20:31,932 --> 00:20:32,933
We have

239
00:20:33,642 --> 00:20:36,186
always been supporting each other
from a distance, right?

240
00:20:39,982 --> 00:20:41,108
How about...

241
00:20:43,318 --> 00:20:44,528
we stay by each other's side

242
00:20:45,195 --> 00:20:46,613
from now on?

243
00:20:50,701 --> 00:20:51,702
Sorry?

244
00:20:56,415 --> 00:20:58,292
I want to start dating you.

245
00:20:58,917 --> 00:20:59,918
Da-reum.

246
00:21:03,797 --> 00:21:04,798
I want

247
00:21:06,258 --> 00:21:07,426
to get to know you more.

248
00:21:25,527 --> 00:21:27,029
I thought you were
hitting it off with the CEO.

249
00:21:27,112 --> 00:21:28,572
What's this plot twist?

250
00:21:28,655 --> 00:21:32,284
Did Chan really ask you out first?

251
00:21:34,244 --> 00:21:35,245
Yes.

252
00:21:40,125 --> 00:21:42,586
No way.
This is straight out of Notting Hill.

253
00:21:44,046 --> 00:21:46,632
I can't believe Chan is
Namda's first potential boyfriend.

254
00:21:47,341 --> 00:21:51,136
This is why you should
never give up on something.

255
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:53,514
So? What did you say to him?

256
00:21:56,266 --> 00:21:57,684
I haven't said anything.

257
00:21:57,935 --> 00:21:59,019
I'm still thinking about it.

258
00:21:59,686 --> 00:22:02,147
You're thinking?
Why would you do that?

259
00:22:03,106 --> 00:22:06,068
I also want to know
what he's really like

260
00:22:06,235 --> 00:22:08,904
not as a celebrity,
but a real person.

261
00:22:10,072 --> 00:22:14,201
But if I rushed into this,
I might ruin all my great memories.

262
00:22:15,911 --> 00:22:18,247
I got a bit scared.

263
00:22:26,129 --> 00:22:28,465
Try going on three dates.

264
00:22:31,969 --> 00:22:34,012
It's not something
you can conclude by thinking.

265
00:22:36,974 --> 00:22:38,100
You should

266
