00:40:04,854 --> 00:40:06,230
I got a muscle cramp.

531
00:40:07,773 --> 00:40:08,983
Maybe you were too immersed.

532
00:40:19,452 --> 00:40:20,703
Oh, Chan.

533
00:40:20,995 --> 00:40:23,080
What about the knot?
Have you had a chance to practice?

534
00:40:23,414 --> 00:40:24,415
Of course.

535
00:40:24,874 --> 00:40:26,876
I practiced it like five times today
every time I had a chance.

536
00:40:26,959 --> 00:40:28,461
What? Really?

537
00:40:30,129 --> 00:40:33,758
What? Are you worried
that I might ruin your first project?

538
00:40:33,841 --> 00:40:35,676
Yes. I'd better check.

539
00:40:36,969 --> 00:40:38,054
When?

540
00:40:38,512 --> 00:40:40,598
No, I was just joking.

541
00:40:43,392 --> 00:40:44,560
It's a cat.

542
00:40:54,779 --> 00:40:56,572
He must be cold.

543
00:40:56,989 --> 00:40:57,990
I know.

544
00:40:59,367 --> 00:41:01,535
He's cute. He's still a baby.

545
00:41:03,454 --> 00:41:04,664
They're kittens.

546
00:41:05,039 --> 00:41:06,791
I can't just leave them here.

547
00:41:06,916 --> 00:41:08,876
Then I'll keep them for now.

548
00:41:15,508 --> 00:41:16,759
- What's wrong?
- What?

549
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:21,472
He reminds me of a cat I know.

550
00:41:24,350 --> 00:41:25,393
Hi.

551
00:41:28,980 --> 00:41:30,731
Do you want to grab something hot
over there?

552
00:41:31,399 --> 00:41:32,817
Oh, yes.

553
00:41:44,412 --> 00:41:46,580
They requested a change
to the contract terms

554
00:41:46,664 --> 00:41:48,666
but it's difficult for us
to accept it.

555
00:41:48,749 --> 00:41:50,292
I'll persuade them myself in person.

556
00:41:50,376 --> 00:41:52,378
Please check
the investor's schedule again.

557
00:41:52,461 --> 00:41:53,462
Okay, Mr. Kang.

558
00:42:01,095 --> 00:42:02,430
This is obstruction of business.

559
00:42:03,556 --> 00:42:04,682
Is it warm here?

560
00:42:14,775 --> 00:42:16,110
About your owner

561
00:42:16,694 --> 00:42:17,987
who did she go meet?

562
00:42:20,197 --> 00:42:21,365
She's taking so long.

563
00:42:28,956 --> 00:42:30,750
- Soybean milk?
- Sounds good.

564
00:42:32,543 --> 00:42:33,586
It's warm.

565
00:42:35,629 --> 00:42:39,508
Excuse me. Aren't you Lee Chan?

566
00:42:40,051 --> 00:42:41,677
- I...
- Right?

567
00:42:42,178 --> 00:42:43,846
I'm a big fan of yours.

568
00:42:44,305 --> 00:42:46,098
It's really him. Awesome.

569
00:42:48,225 --> 00:42:51,353
And she's...

570
00:42:55,858 --> 00:42:56,942
I'm...

571
00:42:58,778 --> 00:43:00,279
Excuse me.

572
00:43:01,363 --> 00:43:03,282
I'm just a passerby.

573
00:43:04,992 --> 00:43:06,285
- You're so hot.
- You're so handsome.

574
00:43:06,368 --> 00:43:07,620
- Can I have a picture?
- How are you so hot?

575
00:43:07,703 --> 00:43:10,623
- You're crazy good-looking.
- My heart is going to explode.

576
00:43:10,706 --> 00:43:12,124
You're unbelievably hot.

577
00:43:12,208 --> 00:43:14,668
Oh, my heart is going to explode.
Let me join.

578
00:43:15,294 --> 00:43:16,504
This is crazy.

579
00:43:29,308 --> 00:43:32,686
His life must be tough.

580
00:43:39,193 --> 00:43:40,236
Gosh, it's cold.

581
00:43:47,743 --> 00:43:49,245
It is him. He's still there.

582
00:43:49,995 --> 00:43:51,163
Awesome.

583
00:43:51,330 --> 00:43:53,124
What a treat to see
Chan in his plain clothes.

584
00:43:53,332 --> 00:43:54,542
But is he alone?

585
00:43:54,750 --> 00:43:56,752
I heard he was seen with someone
in the theater.

586
00:43:56,836 --> 00:43:58,254
- With whom?
- A woman.

587
00:43:58,504 --> 00:44:00,089
If I get in the picture with him

588
00:44:00,422 --> 00:44:01,841
that'll get him in trouble.

589
00:44:05,427 --> 00:44:06,971
Chan, can I have a selfie with you?

590
00:44:07,304 --> 00:44:10,015
- It's really him.
- He's so hot. I can't believe it.

591
00:44:10,099 --> 00:44:11,392
Don't go.

592
00:44:11,475 --> 00:44:12,977
- You're so hot.
- Excuse me. Sorry.

593
00:44:13,060 --> 00:44:14,395
Where are you going?

594
00:44:26,699 --> 00:44:28,075
He must be somewhere nearby.

595
00:44:28,367 --> 00:44:30,119
But he seemed different today.

596
00:44:30,202 --> 00:44:31,829
Didn't he look like he had company?

597
00:44:31,912 --> 00:44:34,748
- Right?
- See this? It's that place.

598
00:44:36,292 --> 00:44:39,378
Oh, how did I miss him?

599
00:44:41,005 --> 00:44:42,756
Right. Look at that.

600
00:45:09,450 --> 00:45:10,784
I barely lost them.

601
00:45:11,327 --> 00:45:12,453
Where did Da-reum go?

602
00:45:16,373 --> 00:45:17,458
DA-REUM

603
00:45:17,917 --> 00:45:22,004
Chan, I think we should
split up for today.

604
00:45:22,379 --> 00:45:24,215
Still, I had a good time.

605
00:45:24,506 --> 00:45:26,884
I have work to do.
I'll head home first.

606
00:45:42,483 --> 00:45:44,401
I feel bad
to send you home like this.

607
00:45:49,823 --> 00:45:53,285
"I'm really fine."

608
00:46:02,253 --> 00:46:04,129
Why do I keep saying I'm okay?

609
00:46:09,885 --> 00:46:11,470
I'm clearly not okay.

610
00:46:21,981 --> 00:46:24,650
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

611
00:46:25,734 --> 00:46:26,735
Hello?

612
00:46:29,571 --> 00:46:31,073
Well...

613
00:46:32,491 --> 00:46:33,784
Ms. Da-reum.

614
00:46:34,076 --> 00:46:35,077
Are you

615
00:46:36,245 --> 00:46:37,621
still busy?

616
00:46:37,705 --> 00:46:40,207
What? Is something wrong?

617
00:46:43,085 --> 00:46:44,169
That is...

618
00:46:49,508 --> 00:46:50,968
The cats.

619
00:46:54,513 --> 00:46:57,391
One of them sleeps too much.

620
00:46:57,850 --> 00:46:59,268
I don't know much about cats.

621
00:46:59,768 --> 00:47:02,604
I thought you should look into them.

622
00:47:02,688 --> 00:47:03,772
Really?

623
00:47:04,398 --> 00:47:05,941
I'll be there soon.

624
00:47:14,783 --> 00:47:15,784
Okay.

625
00:47:16,452 --> 00:47:18,287
They were sleeping until now.

626
00:47:19,830 --> 00:47:21,790
It's not a lie.

627
00:47:34,636 --> 00:47:37,973
I'm sorry. I hope I'm not too late.

628
00:47:38,057 --> 00:47:39,391
Oh, no.

629
00:47:41,310 --> 00:47:42,770
Why do you look so cold?

630
00:47:44,438 --> 00:47:46,523
It's pretty cold.

631
00:47:49,443 --> 00:47:50,944
I hope I didn't disturb you

632
00:47:51,820 --> 00:47:52,821
when you were having fun.

633
00:47:53,322 --> 00:47:54,907
Oh, not at all.

634
00:47:55,657 --> 00:47:56,658
Where are the cats?

635
00:47:56,992 --> 00:47:57,993
Upstairs. Come with me.

636
00:48:09,713 --> 00:48:10,798
So cute.

637
00:48:15,636 --> 00:48:17,262
Drink this and warm up before you go.

638
00:48:17,346 --> 00:48:18,931
Oh, thank you.

639
00:48:24,269 --> 00:48:26,480
- Are you okay?
- Yes, thank you.

640
00:48:30,150 --> 00:48:31,610
Did they just sleep the whole time?

641
00:48:38,325 --> 00:48:39,827
After I hung up the phone

642
00:48:40,744 --> 00:48:42,955
they ate and played just fine.

643
00:48:44,540 --> 00:48:45,666
That's good.

644
00:48:46,208 --> 00:48:48,502
Thank you
for watching the kittens today.

645
00:48:49,378 --> 00:48:50,421
Don't mention it.

646
00:48:52,089 --> 00:48:54,758
They really hit it off
and seemed to have fun.

647
00:48:56,260 --> 00:48:57,386
They hit it off?

648
00:48:59,388 --> 00:49:01,348
Then I should name one Kung

649
00:49:01,432 --> 00:49:04,059
and the other one Jjak, right?

650
00:49:04,143 --> 00:49:06,019
The big one will be Jjak.

651
00:49:06,228 --> 00:49:07,396
The small one will be Kung.

652
00:49:08,063 --> 00:49:09,231
Kung and Jjak.

653
00:49:10,607 --> 00:49:11,608
That works.

654
00:49:14,528 --> 00:49:17,948
But I think you should separate them
for a while.

655
00:49:18,449 --> 00:49:21,368
- Why is that?
- Kung keeps eating Jjak's food.

656
00:49:22,536 --> 00:49:24,788
When you leave home for work,
Jjak will end up starving.

657
00:49:25,205 --> 00:49:27,708
I'll watch Kung for a while.

658
00:49:28,792 --> 00:49:29,918
Really?

659
00:49:31,086 --> 00:49:32,796
Thank you so much, Mr. Kang.

660
00:49:35,132 --> 00:49:37,509
And I've grown
attached to them already.

661
00:49:43,182 --> 00:49:45,309
Do you watch Bitter Sweet too?

662
00:49:45,684 --> 00:49:46,894
Because Director Lee is
starring in it.

663
00:49:47,436 --> 00:49:50,898
I watch them at once to see
if anything might raise an issue.

664
00:49:56,778 --> 00:49:58,780
I feel like
this is a one-sided crush.

665
00:49:58,864 --> 00:50:00,407
That's not true.

666
00:50:00,491 --> 00:50:01,742
I like you too.

667
00:50:02,367 --> 00:50:04,036
I'm just not good
at expressing myself.

668
00:50:05,245 --> 00:50:06,788
You have to say it.

669
00:50:08,999 --> 00:50:10,000
I love you.

670
00:50:13,629 --> 00:50:14,671
I love you.

671
00:50:16,423 --> 00:50:17,424
What was that?

672
00:50:18,217 --> 00:50:19,259
I love you.

673
00:50:19,718 --> 00:50:21,011
I love you, too.

674
00:50:22,429 --> 00:50:23,555
I'm jealous.

675
00:50:25,682 --> 00:50:26,725
Of what?

676
00:50:29,144 --> 00:50:32,064
She can be pouty and sullen

677
00:50:32,523 --> 00:50:33,649
in front of the person she likes.

678
00:50:34,191 --> 00:50:35,192
You are

679
00:50:36,318 --> 00:50:37,319
jealous of that?

680
00:50:39,363 --> 00:50:41,448
That shows how close they are.

681
00:50:44,826 --> 00:50:46,745
When I like someone

682
00:50:47,079 --> 00:50:49,456
I tend to keep it to myself.

683
00:50:50,082 --> 00:50:53,919
But sometimes
I wish I could show how I feel.

684
00:51:06,223 --> 00:51:07,474
Wanting that much

685
00:51:08,892 --> 00:51:10,352
sounds like
a very healthy relationship.

686
00:51:12,396 --> 00:51:13,397
Right?

687
00:51:16,900 --> 00:51:18,193
I'm sorry, Ms. Da-reum.

688
00:51:18,902 --> 00:51:20,279
I can't accept your heart.

689
00:51:20,946 --> 00:51:21,947
If only

690
00:51:22,823 --> 00:51:24,324
I hadn't been a CEO.

691
00:51:26,493 --> 00:51:28,412
No, Kang Ha-gi.

692
00:51:28,912 --> 00:51:29,955
Don't be swayed.

693
00:51:55,939 --> 00:51:57,608
Here.

694
00:51:59,693 --> 00:52:01,820
The house must feel strange
to you, Jjak.

695
00:52:03,030 --> 00:52:04,740
This is where
you're going to stay for a while.

696
00:52:08,744 --> 00:52:11,204
I pretended to be fine

697
00:52:11,622 --> 00:52:13,290
but I was
actually very nervous today.

698
00:52:17,210 --> 00:52:19,129
I'm comfortable around Mr. Kang

699
00:52:19,838 --> 00:52:21,882
but why can't I do the same
with Chan?

700
00:52:24,509 --> 00:52:25,552
Right?

701
00:52:26,053 --> 00:52:27,929
Answer me, Jjak.

702
00:52:36,480 --> 00:52:39,066
Sounds good.
Then let's have dinner on Saturday.

703
00:52:39,149 --> 00:52:40,525
Okay.

704
00:52:52,287 --> 00:52:53,830
You look happy these days.

705
00:52:54,915 --> 00:52:57,918
Is it going well
with Da-reum or something?

706
00:53:00,170 --> 00:53:01,171
Cho-yi.

707
00:53:01,630 --> 00:53:03,465
Stop minding my private life

708
00:53:04,049 --> 00:53:05,717
and focus on your acting.

709
00:53:08,512 --> 00:53:09,763
Chan.

710
00:53:09,846 --> 00:53:12,683
Don't you know that any scandal
you get caught in affects me too?

711
00:53:14,726 --> 00:53:17,229
Stay low
until the show's over, will you?

712
00:53:20,774 --> 00:53:22,109
Just kidding.

713
00:53:22,192 --> 00:53:24,986
You wouldn't date your fan.

714
00:53:27,864 --> 00:53:30,409
- We're ready for the next scene.
- Okay.

715
00:53:34,621 --> 00:53:37,999
Let's go. We've got to love
each other beautifully again today.

716
00:54:04,776 --> 00:54:05,986
The woman of the day.

717
00:54:06,403 --> 00:54:10,115
This is for Ms. Nam Da-reum
who's in charge of the knot event.

718
00:54:10,699 --> 00:54:11,867
Get everything you want.

719
00:54:11,950 --> 00:54:13,702
Oh, I'm not in charge.

720
00:54:13,785 --> 00:54:15,579
I'm just the youngest member.

721
00:54:16,163 --> 00:54:19,124
It's not common for the youngest
to lead a big project like this.

722
00:54:19,207 --> 00:54:22,294
Everyone helped me.

723
00:54:22,544 --> 00:54:25,881
- Not to mention you, too.
- You're welcome.

724
00:54:26,423 --> 00:54:27,549
- Now, take a look.
- Okay.

725
00:54:34,222 --> 00:54:35,849
This is...

726
00:54:35,974 --> 00:54:37,642
It's not even English.

727
00:54:38,477 --> 00:54:39,770
What does it say?

728
00:54:40,061 --> 00:54:41,688
How come there are no pictures?

729
00:54:48,570 --> 00:54:51,823
- Are you ready?
- One second.

730
00:54:52,365 --> 00:54:55,786
- Do you need help?
- Oh, it's okay.

731
00:54:57,162 --> 00:54:59,581
It's not okay.

732
00:54:59,664 --> 00:55:01,291
Just ask him for help.

733
00:55:01,625 --> 00:55:03,168
Do you like fish or steak?

734
00:55:06,755 --> 00:55:09,382
I'm okay with anything.

735
00:55:12,093 --> 00:55:14,304
I like meat.

736
00:55:15,931 --> 00:55:17,140
Do you want me to order?

737
00:55:18,809 --> 00:55:19,893
Yes, please.

738
00:55:24,314 --> 00:55:25,732
We'll get the dinner course

739
00:55:25,816 --> 00:55:28,985
with bass and strip steak.

740
00:55:29,361 --> 00:55:31,988
Has the wine I asked for last time
been aerated?

741
00:55:32,072 --> 00:55:34,407
- Yes, I'll prepare it for you.
- Thank you.

742
00:55:37,994 --> 00:55:40,038
I ordered different dishes
so we can share.

743
00:55:40,121 --> 00:55:41,456
Sure. I'd love to.

744
00:55:48,421 --> 00:55:49,548
Hello.

745
00:55:49,965 --> 00:55:51,174
I made a reservation
under Kang Ha-gi.

746
00:55:51,967 --> 00:55:53,426
This way, please.

747
00:56:00,350 --> 00:56:01,893
This is a very nice restaurant.

748
00:56:04,855 --> 00:56:05,939
Ms. Da-reum?

749
00:56:23,707 --> 00:56:25,166
You must've been flustered last time.

750
00:56:26,042 --> 00:56:27,043
What?

751
00:56:27,711 --> 00:56:30,755
You had to leave
when my fans suddenly rushed over.

752
00:56:31,131 --> 00:56:32,215
I'm sorry.

753
00:56:35,552 --> 00:56:36,678
Don't mind it.

754
00:56:36,761 --> 00:56:39,764
They're all your fans just like me.

755
00:56:41,099 --> 00:56:42,183
I understand.

756
00:56:43,602 --> 00:56:44,644
Still...

757
00:56:46,813 --> 00:56:47,898
Da-reum

758
00:56:48,189 --> 00:56:49,649
you're different to me.

759
00:56:51,109 --> 00:56:52,402
Like I said last time

760
00:56:53,028 --> 00:56:54,529
I was able to endure
the hardest time of my life

761
00:56:55,113 --> 00:56:56,781
thanks to your photo book.

762
00:57:00,368 --> 00:57:01,494
Chan

763
00:57:02,287 --> 00:57:04,789
are you okay now?

764
00:57:05,832 --> 00:57:06,833
What do you mean?

765
00:57:09,544 --> 00:57:11,046
About having
a countless number of people

766
00:57:11,421 --> 00:57:13,423
who love you

767
00:57:13,882 --> 00:57:16,551
look for you,
and look forward to seeing you.

768
00:57:17,344 --> 00:57:18,762
Things like that.

769
00:57:21,097 --> 00:57:22,307
Do you want to know the truth?

770
00:57:28,855 --> 00:57:30,065
Sometimes it's tough.

771
00:57:31,232 --> 00:57:32,442
And it's overwhelming.

772
00:57:35,362 --> 00:57:36,738
As much as people love me

773
00:57:36,821 --> 00:57:39,366
I feel like I have to do well
and prove myself.

774
00:57:40,408 --> 00:57:43,578
I'm afraid one mistake would bring
everything down.

775
00:57:51,544 --> 00:57:54,089
WON-BIN

776
00:57:58,093 --> 00:58:00,887
Maybe something urgent came up.

777
00:58:01,680 --> 00:58:02,889
No, it's fine.

778
00:58:08,311 --> 00:58:09,980
COCOTALK

779
00:58:10,063 --> 00:58:11,982
Chan, it's urgent. Answer your phone.

780
00:58:13,566 --> 00:58:15,026
- Chan.
- Yes.

781
00:58:15,110 --> 00:58:16,736
Why weren't you answering your phone?

782
00:58:16,820 --> 00:58:18,446
I'm outside right now.

783
00:58:19,072 --> 00:58:20,156
What's up?

784
00:58:20,865 --> 00:58:24,035
Director Park Chan-dong
gave us a call.

785
00:58:24,452 --> 00:58:26,496
He wants to see you
at his studio right now.

786
00:58:26,579 --> 00:58:28,081
I guess he liked you at the audition.

787
00:58:28,248 --> 00:58:29,332
Really?

788
00:58:34,129 --> 00:58:35,505
But not now.

789
00:58:37,590 --> 00:58:38,842
This is more important.

790
00:58:38,925 --> 00:58:40,301
Hey. Are you nuts?

791
00:58:40,385 --> 00:58:41,761
This is
a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

792
00:58:42,012 --> 00:58:44,681
This could get you to Cannes.

793
00:58:45,140 --> 00:58:47,267
No more nonsense. Wrap it up now.

794
00:58:47,642 --> 00:58:49,102
I'll go pick you up now.

795
00:59:05,285 --> 00:59:06,995
Da-reum, I'm sorry...

796
00:59:09,831 --> 00:59:11,207
Do you have to go?

797
00:59:11,291 --> 00:59:13,501
A meeting just got scheduled
for my next project.

798
00:59:14,502 --> 00:59:16,504
That's really important.

799
00:59:16,588 --> 00:59:19,257
The director's only available
right now.

800
00:59:19,340 --> 00:59:20,341
I'm sorry.

801
00:59:20,550 --> 00:59:22,927
Oh, no. It's okay.

802
00:59:23,344 --> 00:59:24,679
Like you said earlier

803
00:59:24,929 --> 00:59:27,307
you have to prove yourself
as much as you're loved.

804
00:59:27,807 --> 00:59:29,059
Sorry about this, Da-reum.

805
00:59:30,351 --> 00:59:32,979
It's really okay.
You should get going.

806
00:59:33,521 --> 00:59:35,440
- I'll call you.
- Yes.

807
00:59:39,736 --> 00:59:40,737
Go on.

808
01:00:29,577 --> 01:00:32,372
Your party
had arranged this in advance.

809
01:00:47,554 --> 01:00:49,389
MS. NAM DA-REUM
HAPPY BIRTHDAY

810
01:00:52,183 --> 01:00:53,351
What's she doing alone?

811
01:00:54,060 --> 01:00:56,312
She's looking this way.

812
01:00:56,479 --> 01:00:59,315
That's sad.

813
01:01:00,900 --> 01:01:02,819
HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO NAM DA-REUM

814
01:01:13,621 --> 01:01:15,915
Wait, no one showed up for real?

815
01:01:15,999 --> 01:01:17,417
LEE YE-JI

816
01:01:17,959 --> 01:01:18,960
Sorry.

817
01:01:19,210 --> 01:01:21,546
Hey. I told you. That place is lame.

818
01:01:21,629 --> 01:01:23,423
The master of playing by herself.

819
01:01:23,506 --> 01:01:25,717
Nam Da-reum's
legendary solo birthday party.

820
01:01:35,059 --> 01:01:37,562
Are your friends running late?

821
01:01:39,814 --> 01:01:40,982
They'll be here soon.

822
01:01:42,108 --> 01:01:43,234
It's okay.

823
01:02:11,429 --> 01:02:12,472
Mr. Kang.

824
01:02:13,514 --> 01:02:15,516
- Get up.
- Sorry?

825
01:02:30,281 --> 01:02:31,282
Ms. Nam.

826
01:02:33,159 --> 01:02:34,244
Have you been

827
01:02:35,912 --> 01:02:37,247
going on blind dates by any chance?

828
01:02:37,789 --> 01:02:39,624
Blind dates?

829
01:02:39,958 --> 01:02:41,501
Last time, when you asked me
to watch the cats

830
01:02:42,627 --> 01:02:43,711
and even today.

831
01:02:45,421 --> 01:02:46,422
Oh, right.

832
01:02:46,756 --> 01:02:48,466
Yes, it's a blind date.

833
01:02:49,259 --> 01:02:51,219
If you're trying to get over
someone you like

834
01:02:52,887 --> 01:02:53,888
don't bother.

835
01:02:55,890 --> 01:02:57,058
You don't need

836
01:02:58,393 --> 01:02:59,769
to let go of your feelings.

837
01:03:01,854 --> 01:03:03,898
Okay.

838
01:03:05,149 --> 01:03:07,110
Anyway, did he leave without you?

839
01:03:09,320 --> 01:03:10,405
Well...

840
01:03:11,239 --> 01:03:13,825
I was kind of flustered too.

841
01:03:14,575 --> 01:03:16,786
But it happens.

842
01:03:19,539 --> 01:03:22,083
- I'm okay.
- But you're not.

843
01:03:25,086 --> 01:03:26,296
You always say

844
01:03:27,380 --> 01:03:28,423
you're okay.

845
01:03:30,258 --> 01:03:32,260
I guess people won't feel as bad
when you say that.

846
01:03:33,553 --> 01:03:35,054
But you're hurt.

847
01:03:36,639 --> 01:03:37,765
At least, in front of me

848
01:03:39,976 --> 01:03:41,311
you can say it's not okay.

849
01:03:48,318 --> 01:03:49,319
Okay.

850
01:03:50,611 --> 01:03:51,612
To be honest

851
01:03:53,531 --> 01:03:54,824
it wasn't okay.

852
01:03:56,743 --> 01:03:57,910
It's okay.

853
01:04:01,331 --> 01:04:03,207
When I pretend to be okay

854
01:04:07,837 --> 01:04:08,838
I look

855
01:04:11,090 --> 01:04:12,759
less pitiful.

856
01:04:14,969 --> 01:04:17,597
"I'm really fine."

857
01:04:20,016 --> 01:04:22,268
It's really okay.
You should get going.

858
01:04:26,856 --> 01:04:28,733
I've always swallowed it.

859
01:04:30,777 --> 01:04:33,363
But today, it kind of hurts.

860
01:04:33,946 --> 01:04:35,615
Don't meet anyone like that.

861
01:04:38,409 --> 01:04:39,494
Ms. Nam Da-reum.

862
01:04:40,119 --> 01:04:41,662
You deserve better than that.

863
01:04:43,581 --> 01:04:47,251
You don't deserve to date a jerk

864
01:04:48,669 --> 01:04:49,962
who leaves you on a blind date.

865
01:04:58,846 --> 01:05:02,016
That jerk is your friend.

866
01:05:03,309 --> 01:05:04,352
Why are you smiling?

867
01:05:08,147 --> 01:05:10,149
No, it's nothing.

868
01:05:15,488 --> 01:05:18,032
Maybe something more important
than me came up.

869
01:05:19,784 --> 01:05:21,494
Still, for some reason

870
01:05:22,578 --> 01:05:23,871
it's less disappointing today.

871
01:05:24,956 --> 01:05:26,958
Perhaps because I'm walking with you.

872
01:05:29,502 --> 01:05:30,753
I think

873
01:05:31,921 --> 01:05:33,339
I feel better.

874
01:05:34,048 --> 01:05:35,341
The air is nice.

875
01:05:38,136 --> 01:05:39,887
This is a lot better
than the blind date.

876
01:05:47,353 --> 01:05:48,646
I should go home

877
01:05:50,273 --> 01:05:51,482
but I don't want to.

878
01:05:52,150 --> 01:05:53,192
Why not?

879
01:05:56,946 --> 01:05:57,947
Because

880
01:06:00,199 --> 01:06:01,868
I want to stay like this.

881
01:06:03,161 --> 01:06:04,203
Sorry?

882
01:06:07,415 --> 01:06:08,583
Because of Kung.

883
01:06:09,333 --> 01:06:11,752
He doesn't stop running at night
as if he's possessed.

884
01:06:13,296 --> 01:06:14,464
Jjak too.

885
01:06:15,423 --> 01:06:18,426
Apparently, when they're kittens,
they have too much energy to handle.

886
01:06:18,843 --> 01:06:21,637
If Jjak doesn't sleep during the day,
he runs so much at dawn.

887
01:06:21,721 --> 01:06:23,598
So I keep waking up at dawn.

888
01:06:23,973 --> 01:06:26,267
If they live together,
it'll be war every day.

889
01:06:27,268 --> 01:06:28,311
But then

890
01:06:28,769 --> 01:06:31,314
if they stay together,
they'll be less lonely.

891
01:06:36,944 --> 01:06:38,279
This is Jjak from earlier today.

892
01:06:38,613 --> 01:06:41,240
He was enjoying the sunlight,
then he dozed off.

893
01:06:41,782 --> 01:06:43,117
Just like the owner.

894
01:06:43,868 --> 01:06:46,162
So bright and gentle.

895
01:07:01,594 --> 01:07:03,471
It's the first snow this season.

896
01:07:05,681 --> 01:07:06,933
It's pretty.

897
01:07:12,939 --> 01:07:13,981
Yes.

898
01:07:16,025 --> 01:07:17,193
So pretty.

899
01:07:57,817 --> 01:08:01,529
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

900
01:08:11,747 --> 01:08:14,000
Do you want to meet outside?

901
01:08:14,458 --> 01:08:17,211
How can Mr. Kang be fine?

902
01:08:17,295 --> 01:08:18,629
He's such a pro.

903
01:08:19,046 --> 01:08:21,299
To be honest... Wait!

904
01:08:21,382 --> 01:08:24,218
I liked him for a very long time.

905
01:08:24,594 --> 01:08:25,636
LA?

906
01:08:25,720 --> 01:08:27,054
Why don't you come with me?

907
01:08:27,221 --> 01:08:28,681
Whoever he is

908
01:08:28,764 --> 01:08:31,058
you don't need to put up
with him that much.

909
01:08:31,142 --> 01:08:32,852
Are you protecting your employee

910
01:08:32,935 --> 01:08:34,061
or are you keeping me in check?

911
01:08:34,854 --> 01:08:37,023
Mr. Kang, the truth is...

912
01:08:37,356 --> 01:08:39,066
- Is this...
- Chan, where are you going?

913
01:08:39,275 --> 01:08:40,401
Is this true?

